course: dictionary
lesson: 14323
title: Words that shock
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: An obscenity is a very rude or offensive word, especially a swear word. You will usually see it in the plural, obscenities, when people shout them. «The man shouted obscenities at the referee and was sent off.» The clue is shouted and sent off: the words were rude and not allowed.
explain: The word can also mean something shockingly rude or offensive, like a picture or a joke that is meant to upset people. «The graffiti was an obscenity on the school wall.» Here the clue is on the school wall: the writing was rude and should not be there.
explain: Adults and writers also use obscenity for something morally shocking, meaning very wrong. «War is an obscenity» does not mean war is rude. It means war is deeply wrong and cruel. Ask yourself: is the writer talking about bad words, or about something that is just wrong? The sentence around the word tells you.
fact: An obscenity is a noun, so you can say «an obscenity» or «obscenities».
fact: «Obscenity» means a very rude or offensive word, or something shockingly rude.
fact: Some words are not allowed at school, because they are rude and can hurt or upset people.
fact: «Obscenity» can also mean something morally shocking or wrong, such as «the obscenity of hunger in a rich world».
fact: Common phrases are «shout obscenities» and «an obscenity».
exercise: «The man shouted obscenities at the referee and was sent off.» What does obscenities mean? | Kind comments | *Very rude, offensive words | Loud songs | Long speeches
exercise: «The poverty in that city is an obscenity.» Does the writer mean a rude word? | Yes, it means a funny joke | *No, the writer means it is shocking and morally wrong | No, it means a cosy picnic | Yes, it means a swear word
exercise: Which verb goes best with obscenities? | Sing | *Shout | Plant | Bake
test:
«The children were told that obscenities are not allowed in the playground.» What does this sentence suggest? | *Rude, offensive words are not allowed | Singing is not allowed | Playing games is not allowed | Eating lunch outside is not allowed
test:
«Hunger in a rich world is an obscenity.» What does the writer mean? | A small, funny joke | A rare kind of food | Something quiet and gentle | *Something shocking and deeply wrong
exam:
«The graffiti was an obscenity on the school wall, so the head teacher ordered it cleaned.» What does the word obscenity mean here? | A cosy picnic | A kind of weather | *Something shockingly rude or offensive | A small, quiet bird
